[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
Router4 and the Location C network are operating normally. Evidence: from PC11 the default gateway 192.168.200.1 responds (2/2 pings). Other C-office hosts (PC12/PC13/PC14) also successfully ping 192.168.200.1. Inter-site reachability works (PC11 -> 172.16.10.4 succeeds). On router4, eth0 (LAN) is UP with 192.168.200.1/24, and uplinks eth4 (192.168.15.2/24) and eth5 (172.25.1.1/24) are UP. FRR is running (zebra and ripd), router4 has a valid default via 172.25.1.2 and multiple RIP-learned routes, and its FIB shows C-office LAN directly connected. Router4’s uptime is ~1d21h (no recent crash/reboot).

Mechanism: If the router were down or its LAN interface failed, PCs would not reach 192.168.200.1 nor remote subnets; both are currently reachable. This indicates the gateway and upstream routing are healthy.

Localization: No fault on router4 or its connected interfaces (eth0/eth4/eth5). Local switching between PC11/12/13/14 and router4 is also functioning.

Root cause: The reported outage cannot be reproduced; likely a transient local issue or misinterpretation on site rather than a router4 failure.

Corrective fix: None required on router4. If issues recur at desks, verify individual host configs/cabling and the local access switches (switch5/switch6) for port errors or flaps. We’ll keep monitoring router4, but the site is presently operational. === END ===